> <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`Tail.forInRev` from `j₀ - 1` down to `lo` instead of from `hi - 1`. It is specified by\n`Tail.forInRevFrom_eq`.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/ISize/Program.html#ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail.forInRevFrom","kind":"def","line":1023,"name":"ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail.forInRevFrom","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/ISize/Program.lean#L1023-L1033"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/ISize/Program.html#ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail.forIn\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">ISizeArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">InPlace</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tail</span>.<span class=\"name\">forIn</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">γ</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> w}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> v}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">lo </span><span class=\"fn\">hi</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">init</span> : <span class=\"fn\">β</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">body</span> : <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">j</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a>) → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">lo</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux.html#USize.toNat\">toNat</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LE.le\">≤</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">j</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux.html#USize.toNat\">toNat</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">j</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux.html#USize.toNat\">toNat</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LT.lt\">&lt;</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">hi</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux.html#USize.toNat\">toNat</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">β</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./ScalarArray/ISize/Program.html#ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail\">Tail</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span>)</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./ScalarArray/ISize/Program.html#ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail\">Tail</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./ScalarArray/ISize/Program.html#ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail\">Tail</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./ScalarArray/ISize/Program.html#ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail\">Tail</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">γ</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"A loop in continuation-passing style, for each `j` from `lo` up to `hi - 1`, followed by the rest\n`k` of the program. The body gets `j`, both its bounds, the continuation `next` and the current\nvariables, and ends by calling `next` on the next variables, which runs the next step, or `k` after\nthe last one. So the variables are arguments of the loop, and a scalar stays unboxed, and a nested\nloop, whose `k` calls the outer `next`, allocates nothing either. A body that doesn't call `next`\nleaves the loop early. `Tail.forIn2`, … `Tail.forIn8` of `ScalarArray.ISize.Loops` take two to\neight variables, each its own argument.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/ISize/Program.html#ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail.forIn","kind":"def","line":987,"name":"ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail.forIn","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/ISize/Program.lean#L987-L1002"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/ISize/Program.html#ScalarArray.ISizeArray.InPlace.Tail.forInFrom\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">ISizeArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">InPlace</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tail</span>.<span class=\"name\">forInFrom</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">γ</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> w}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> v}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">lo </span><span class=\"fn\">hi </span><span class=\"fn\">j₀</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">lo</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux.html#USize.toNat\">toNat</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LE.le\">≤</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">j₀</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux